{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-co-molecular-braid","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:co-molecular-braid","kind":"definition","title":"Carbon monoxide $CO$ as a molecular braid","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-covalent-bond-shared-trefoil"],"tags":["carbon-monoxide","CO","triple-bond","heteronuclear","molecular-braid"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Molecular.COBraid","text":"co-molecular-braid.md","leanSource":"co-molecular-braid.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"def:co-molecular-braid\"></a>\n<strong>Definition.</strong> <em>Carbon monoxide <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">CO</code> as a molecular braid</em></p>\n<p><strong>Definition.</strong>\n<strong>Carbon monoxide</strong> <em><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">CO</code> is the molecular braid of a carbon atom <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">C(6, 6)</code> and an oxygen atom <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">O(8, 8)</code> sharing three electron pairs (triple bond).</em></p>\n"}
